{"id": "EUVD-2026-103975", "enisaUuid": "a768b80a-3b4b-3a82-9cc0-7d22dbcb77a0", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmtd: rawnand: cadence: Initialize IRQ state before requesting IRQ\n\nThe Cadence NAND interrupt handler uses both the IRQ lock and completion\nobject. Registering the IRQ before initializing them leaves a window in\nwhich a pending interrupt can access uninitialized synchronization state.\n\nInitialize them before registering the handler.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:46:56", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:56:03", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c69d8aceda362c95bbc4e2182f5829275a7db0c8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/24319f25b641e55f84e55455092a39a2485c78d4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1ed0ccd5649154bfc00ab11c59262d4f42515252", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bbd87eca5407288f2b63ff9357c611cd57e7e640", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/21f027016b1290d13c30b198ae7a00e6b3d1d5a5"], "aliases": ["GHSA-wr98-xxcm-8gqw", "CVE-2026-98721"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2cc5d234-fd04-3618-ae39-7a41ceb94db9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ec4ba01e894d3165e4d1ccbef782ef5593b708b4 <c69d8aceda362c95bbc4e2182f5829275a7db0c8"}, {"id": "408b0d68-8f70-3ef5-91fe-aa58cde2f217", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ec4ba01e894d3165e4d1ccbef782ef5593b708b4 <24319f25b641e55f84e55455092a39a2485c78d4"}, {"id": "545b52c0-ee89-3af0-a224-ecf92a620767", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "588b3c89-e166-32d6-81d7-e1ee53c8bebb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.5"}, {"id": "86ac0165-1643-38c9-b0b6-b2be86fd91f0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ec4ba01e894d3165e4d1ccbef782ef5593b708b4 <bbd87eca5407288f2b63ff